{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":5,"start_col":20,"end_line":5,"end_col":35,"message":"`as_writer` takes a `Cap(IO.Console)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.\nhelp: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `as_writer` may use, give it a `needs` clause.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":5,"start_col":16,"end_line":5,"end_col":35,"text":""},{"kind":"replace","start_line":10,"start_col":23,"end_line":10,"end_col":24,"text":""}],"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":5,"start_col":39,"end_line":5,"end_col":56,"message":"`Cap(IO.FileWrite)` was retired: capability values grant nothing since the current authority replaced them.\nhelp: remove it; code uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":6,"start_col":4,"end_line":6,"end_col":17,"message":"`Cap(IO.Console)` cannot be widened to `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` — `cap_narrow` only attenuates, so the source capability must subsume the target.\nhelp: `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` is not below `Cap(IO.Console)` in the capability lattice. Receive it from a caller that holds an ancestor of it.","code":"cap_widen","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":6,"start_col":4,"end_line":6,"end_col":17,"message":"`cap_narrow` was retired with the capability values it narrowed.\nhelp: remove the call; to run code under less authority, use `restrict SCOPE do ... end`.","code":"cap_narrow_retired","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":9,"start_col":2,"end_line":12,"end_col":5,"message":"`main` is granted `Cap(IO.Console)`, but the program reaches `IO.FileWrite` (reached from `main`: main → as_writer). The grant is a ceiling on the WHOLE program — declaring `needs IO.FileWrite` does not raise it.\nhelp: add `IO.FileWrite` to `main`'s request (its `needs` clause, or the module's `needs` line when `main` has no clause), or request all of `IO`, or remove the use.","code":"cap_grant_exceeded","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/cap_widen_4.march","start_line":9,"start_col":14,"end_line":9,"end_col":29,"message":"`main` asks for its authority with `Cap` parameters, which are deprecated and will be removed in the next release: a capability value grants nothing since the current authority replaced it.\nhelp: request it with a `needs` clause: `fn main() needs IO.Console do`.","code":"deprecated_main_cap","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":9,"start_col":9,"end_line":9,"end_col":30,"text":"()"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":9,"start_col":31,"end_line":9,"end_col":31,"text":"needs IO.Console "}],"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
